  "title": "Unified Title: XDecomposer and XRF-to-Optical Localization",
  "summary": "XDecomposer is a prior-free framework for learning set decomposition in multiphase X-ray diffraction (PXRD) analysis, improving source separation and phase identification compared to existing approaches. It enables accurate, source-resolved multiphase XRD analysis while maintaining crystallographic fidelity. XRF-to-Optical localization using vision language models enhances X-ray fluorescence (XRF) field-of-view (FOV) mapping, addressing challenges in low-correspondence cases.",
